with Braganza.

260
00:14:37,267 --> 00:14:38,867
Good, good.

261
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:43,100
If you fix that on
or before my birthday,

262
00:14:43,233 --> 00:14:45,267
I'll double your cut.

263
00:14:45,400 --> 00:14:47,167
Really, Godfather?

264
00:14:47,300 --> 00:14:49,933
Wow! Thank you so much,
Godfather!

265
00:14:50,067 --> 00:14:51,233
I'll go with that!

266
00:14:51,367 --> 00:14:53,233
So excited!

267
00:14:57,067 --> 00:14:59,700
<i>It's not possible next week,
Andrew.</i>

268
00:14:59,833 --> 00:15:02,367
<i>The client is following up
again.</i>

269
00:15:02,533 --> 00:15:03,800
Wait, can I...

270
00:15:04,833 --> 00:15:06,633
I'll just do what I need
to shoot here.

271
00:15:06,767 --> 00:15:07,967
No, you can't.

272
00:15:08,100 --> 00:15:10,000
They have a technical
requirement.

273
00:15:10,133 --> 00:15:13,100
And then they want you here
on the Tirada Express bus.

274
00:15:14,833 --> 00:15:16,233
<i> Okay, I'll go home.</i>

275
00:15:16,367 --> 00:15:17,267
Okay.

276
00:15:18,733 --> 00:15:20,133
Do you need to leave?

277
00:15:21,500 --> 00:15:22,900
Yes.

278
00:15:23,033 --> 00:15:26,300
I just need to take care
of something for a client, Joey.

279
00:15:26,433 --> 00:15:28,167
I'll be back tomorrow morning.

280
00:15:29,867 --> 00:15:31,300
Okay.

281
00:15:31,433 --> 00:15:32,300
While you're gone,

282
00:15:32,433 --> 00:15:34,833
Peter and I will just go around
with Jin Ho.

283
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:40,200
Okay, and I'll also take care of
the SUV's license plate number.

284
00:15:40,333 --> 00:15:42,333
Be careful.

285
00:15:42,467 --> 00:15:43,533
Okay.

286
00:15:46,600 --> 00:15:48,000
Andrew...

287
00:15:49,667 --> 00:15:51,733
can I ask you a favor?

288
00:15:53,033 --> 00:15:54,967
Sure, what's that?

289
00:15:55,100 --> 00:15:57,433
Can you visit my father?

290
00:15:59,633 --> 00:16:00,633
Of course.

291
00:16:03,033 --> 00:16:04,100
Thank you.

292
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:06,867
Okay.

293
00:16:19,267 --> 00:16:21,067
He's still nowhere to be seen.

294
00:16:21,200 --> 00:16:25,667
Even now, I haven't seen
any news about him.

295
00:16:25,800 --> 00:16:29,300
Miguel, maybe you know where
Diego is.

296
00:16:30,433 --> 00:16:31,767
I don't know.

297
00:16:31,900 --> 00:16:34,267
Miguel, make sure.

298
00:16:34,400 --> 00:16:37,567
Your secrecy won't help you now.

299
00:16:37,700 --> 00:16:39,200
I'm not lying to you.

300
00:16:39,333 --> 00:16:43,000
I'll do anything to get out
of here, to be with you.

301
00:16:44,700 --> 00:16:46,667
My Boss wants to help.

302
00:16:46,800 --> 00:16:49,833
She says her husband
has connections.

303
00:16:49,967 --> 00:16:52,333
She said she can ask him
to look into your case.

304
00:16:53,533 --> 00:16:55,533
Please tell her, thank you.

305
00:16:57,200 --> 00:16:58,633
I'm thinking about nothing
else right now

306
00:16:58,767 --> 00:17:00,300
but your safety and Joey's

307
00:17:02,100 --> 00:17:03,900
because you're important to me.

308
00:17:11,167 --> 00:17:15,800
Elai messaged me, and she said
that you couldn't be reached.

309
00:17:17,300 --> 00:17:20,933
And apparently,
you have a backlog again.

310
00:17:22,033 --> 00:17:27,233
Well, Yvette, I just don't
have a signal where I went.

311
00:17:31,433 --> 00:17:33,600
And where exactly is that?

312
00:17:34,800 --> 00:17:38,267
You're always on the move,
but you're not with your team.

313
00:17:39,400 --> 00:17:40,833
Do you have a girlfriend?

314
00:17:44,733 --> 00:17:46,633
What? Hey!

315
00:17:46,767 --> 00:17:48,167
I'm your sister.

316
00:17:48,300 --> 00:17:51,467
You know, I miss times
like this, you know,

317
00:17:51,633 --> 00:17:55,400
we're just talking about
anything under the sun.

318
00:17:55,533 --> 00:17:56,800
Come on, come on.

319
00:17:56,933 --> 00:17:58,667
Is she pretty?

320
00:17:58,800 --> 00:18:01,000
Yvette, I'm not dating anyone.

321
00:18:03,133 --> 00:18:07,933
But I'm helping someone
with a case.

322
00:18:08,067 --> 00:18:09,133
That's it.

323
00:18:17,867 --> 00:18:19,900
This is so good!

324
00:18:20,033 --> 00:18:21,800
What is it called again?

325
00:18:21,967 --> 00:18:24,500
It has tapa, and then
that's garlic rice...

326
00:18:24,633 --> 00:18:26,767
that's the rice. And then egg,
the egg.

327
00:18:26,900 --> 00:18:28,600
So it's tap-si-log.

328
00:18:28,733 --> 00:18:31,333
- Tapsilog, right?
- Yes.

329
00:18:31,467 --> 00:18:32,767
It's delicious.

330
00:18:32,900 --> 00:18:34,767
Yes, right?

331
00:18:37,200 --> 00:18:38,500
Failed!

332
00:18:38,633 --> 00:18:41,700
No one from the people I've
asked has recognized her yet.

333
00:18:43,267 --> 00:18:46,200
Well, it's still early.
We'll still go around.

334
00:18:48,733 --> 00:18:50,600
- Okay, I'll just pay.
- Okay.

335
00:18:51,733 --> 00:18:53,633
Wait. What's your diet?

336
00:18:54,867 --> 00:18:55,667
How much, Miss?

337
00:18:57,667 --> 00:19:01,133
<i>So what do you like better?
Korean rice or Filipino rice?</i>

338
00:19:02,567 --> 00:19:03,733
Never mind.

339
00:19:17,467 --> 00:19:18,833
<i> Wait!</i>

340
00:19:18,967 --> 00:19:20,367
<i> Hey, move over!</i>

341
00:19:23,567 --> 00:19:25,500
That's Golda's driver.

342
00:19:28,100 --> 00:19:30,567
Are you okay?
Have you paid already?

343
00:19:45,500 --> 00:19:47,900
It's a good thing I saw him
before they left.

344
00:19:48,033 --> 00:19:50,867
It's a good thing we didn't ask
him about Golda,

345
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:52,733
or else we'd be caught.

346
00:19:53,933 --> 00:19:55,600
Let's just follow him.

347
00:19:55,733 --> 00:19:58,867
I'm sure she'll show us
where Golda is.

348
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:00,933
And what is she like?

349
00:20:01,067 --> 00:20:02,300
Is she sweet?

350
00:20:02,467 --> 00:20:03,667
Nice?

351
00:20:03,800 --> 00:20:06,367
Wife material?

352
00:20:06,500 --> 00:20:09,433
She's annoying.

353
00:20:09,567 --> 00:20:12,500
Yvette, we always clash.

354
00:20:12,633 --> 00:20:14,133
She's always hot-tempered,

355
00:20:14,267 --> 00:20:16,133
and I'm the one who always gets
involved.

356
00:20:18,733 --> 00:20:22,000
And her eyes, she'll give you
the intense look.

357
00:20:23,467 --> 00:20:27,100
It's like you're always
being judged.

358
00:20:27,233 --> 00:20:28,400
So grumpy.

359
00:20:31,200 --> 00:20:33,533
You know what's so funny?

360
00:20:33,667 --> 00:20:37,933
You never described
a woman this way.

361
00:20:38,100 --> 00:20:42,967
Usually, all you say is,
okay and kind.

362
00:20:43,100 --> 00:20:44,200
That's it, that's all.

363
00:20:44,333 --> 00:20:47,033
Well, because she's not okay
or kind.

364
00:20:47,167 --> 00:20:49,200
She drives me crazy, actually.

365
00:20:50,300 --> 00:20:52,967
Usually, that's how it starts,
you know.

366
00:20:53,100 --> 00:20:57,167
You fight and argue, and then,
eventually,

367
00:20:57,300 --> 00:21:00,367
you exhaust the worst
of each other

368
00:21:01,400 --> 00:21:04,233
until you see the best
of each other.

369
00:21:05,267 --> 00:21:07,467
Yvette, we're not like that.

370
00:21:08,500 --> 00:21:10,000
Not really.

371
00:21:11,933 --> 00:21:17,633
We have no common ground,
not even a square inch.

372
00:21:17,767 --> 00:21:19,567
Just wait.

373
00:21:19,700 --> 00:21:22,133
There will come a moment,
you know.

374
00:21:22,267 --> 00:21:23,733
A crack in the wall...

375
00:21:24,933 --> 00:21:28,633
A look, then you'll suddenly
realize...

376
00:21:30,067 --> 00:21:33,900
Why does this girl matter a lot?

377
00:21:49,767 --> 00:21:50,967
This is it.

378
00:21:51,100 --> 00:21:52,533
Looks like we're close.

379
00:21:54,067 --> 00:22:04,033
(BACKGROUND SOUNDS)

380
00:22:15,967 --> 00:22:17,667
Are they going to the carnival?

381
00:22:17,800 --> 00:22:19,733
Come on, let's follow.

382
00:22:21,500 --> 00:22:28,800
(BACKGROUND SOUNDS)

383
00:22:29,633 --> 00:22:36,200
(INTENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

384
00:22:36,333 --> 00:22:38,000
Andrew, tell me the truth.

385
00:22:38,133 --> 00:22:40,667
Are you working on an expose
that we don't know about?

386
00:22:40,800 --> 00:22:42,033
I need to keep my distance.

387
00:22:42,167 --> 00:22:44,367
If you're too close,
they will get suspicious again.

388
00:22:44,500 --> 00:22:47,033
That's the M14 and AK-47.

389
00:22:47,167 --> 00:22:48,867
Will you offer that to them,
too?

390
00:22:49,033 --> 00:22:50,067
Exactly.

391
00:22:50,200 --> 00:22:51,933
This is where Golda is hiding?

392
00:22:52,067 --> 00:22:53,700
Wow. You're really good
at your job.

393
00:22:53,833 --> 00:22:56,000
Lucky, I guess.
Are you mad at me?

394
00:22:56,133 --> 00:22:57,867
I'm your best friend, right?

395
00:22:58,000 --> 00:22:59,633
Wow. Clingy?

396
00:22:59,767 --> 00:23:03,300
Fine, so what if I'm clingy?
What can you do? I love you!

397
00:23:03,433 --> 00:23:06,733
Do you know the one they call
Godfather?

398
00:23:06,867 --> 00:23:08,200
That's Vincent Alcala.

399
00:23:08,333 --> 00:23:09,667
Be careful with him.

400
00:23:09,800 --> 00:23:11,533
This is a big syndicate.
